doc Precondition, turned off: require cond checks only the types.
  The same syntax as [check/require](../check/require.md), but the condition and
  messages are never evaluated: the statement compiles to a jump over
  them. Use the `nocheck` truck to switch a whole program's checks off.

needs std/if std/and std/false std/let
syntax statement
  require {c: expr bool} [, {m: expr str}]*
expand
  if false && {c}
    {each g in ,}
    let {cat $m #g} = {g.m}
    {end}
  end
